<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <AssemblyName>SwissEphNet</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>SwissEphNet</RootNamespace>
    <PackageId>SwissEphNet</PackageId>
    <!--
      Version scheme: upstream Swiss Ephemeris version + port revision, e.g.
      2.8.x tracks Swiss Ephemeris C 2.08 with x as this port's own revision
      counter. This is not published to nuget.org: 2.8.0.2 already is, and
      the library no longer ships net40/netstandard1.0, so it would not be a
      drop-in replacement for that package anyway. Distribution is
      source-only (clone/build/reference) until the 2.10.03 port lands. Do
      not bump this to a 2.10.x version before that port actually happens.
    -->
    <Version>2.8.1.0</Version>
    <Authors>Yan Grenier, Timothy van der Ham</Authors>
    <Company>Yan Grenier</Company>
    <Product>SwissEphNet</Product>
    <Description>Swiss Ephemeris .Net portage</Description>
    <Copyright>Copyright (C) 1997-2021 Astrodienst AG; (C) 2014-2019 Yan Grenier; (C) 2026 Timothy van der Ham</Copyright>
    <PackageLicenseUrl></PackageLicenseUrl>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Tim81/SwissEphNet</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Tim81/SwissEphNet</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageTags>Swiss Ephemeris</PackageTags>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>2.8.1.0 (not published to nuget.org; source-only distribution):
- Retarget the library to netstandard2.0;net8.0;net10.0, dropping net40 and netstandard1.0.
- Relicense from GPL-2.0-or-later to the Swiss Ephemeris 2.10.3 dual license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
  or a Swiss Ephemeris Professional License from Astrodienst. See LICENSE and NOTICE.
- Fix SwissEph.DIR_GLUE: was hardcoded to '\\' on every platform, now '/' per the upstream C
  source. Asteroid file names passed to OnLoadFile change accordingly, e.g. "ast4/se04179.se1"
  instead of "ast4\se04179.se1".
- Fix SwissEph.DefaultEncoding: was falling back to UTF-8 silently whenever Windows-1252 could
  not be resolved (missing System.Text.Encoding.CodePages reference); UTF-8 is now the explicit,
  deliberate default, matching the actual encoding of the ephemeris data files.
  You can still override it via the static SwissEphNet.SwissEph.DefaultEncoding property.
- Fix C.strcmp/strncmp/strstr/strchr: were culture-sensitive (string.Compare/IndexOf), now
  ordinal, matching C's byte-wise semantics. Affects fixed-star name search/sort under
  non-invariant cultures.
- Several additional port bug fixes with no signature change: swe_fixstar multi-word star names
  and an off-by-one in search-name formatting, a missing ref-parameter mutation and missing guard
  in the heliacal Moon branch, swe_set_astro_models throwing on short input, C.atoi sign handling,
  CPointer&lt;T&gt;.operator != always returning false, and a netstandard2.0-only infinite
  recursion in a string-extension method. See NOTICE and docs/known-issues.md for details.

2.8.0.2:
- Fix the #41 issue

2.8.0.1:
- Update to version 2.08 of SwissEphemeris

2.7.1.3:
- Update to version 2.07.1 of SwissEphemeris
- Inlcude the PR #34 - swe_house_pos: parameter geolon is actually geolat - thanks to aleksamagicka

2.6.0.24:
- Include the PR #32 - Make fixed star name parameter ref  - thanks to aleksamagicka

2.6.0.23:
- Fix the #29 issue

2.6.0.22:
- Fix the #27 issue

2.6.0.21:
- Update to VS 2017 project

2.6.0.18:
- Update the code to the Swiss Ephemeris 2.06.00 version.
</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <NeutralLanguage>en</NeutralLanguage>
    <!--
      Deliberately PackageLicenseFile, not PackageLicenseExpression. NuGet only
      accepts OSI/FSF-approved SPDX identifiers in PackageLicenseExpression, and
      the Swiss Ephemeris Professional License arm of this dual license has no
      SPDX identifier, so the dual license cannot be expressed that way. Do not
      "fix" this to PackageLicenseExpression=AGPL-3.0-or-later: that would drop
      the Professional option from the package metadata and misrepresent the
      license under which this library is actually offered. See LICENSE and
      NOTICE for the real terms.
    -->
    <PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE</PackageLicenseFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(Configuration)|$(Platform)'=='Debug|AnyCPU'">
    <DefineConstants>TRACE;DEBUG;</DefineConstants>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(Configuration)|$(Platform)'=='Release|AnyCPU'">
    <DefineConstants>TRACE;RELEASE;</DefineConstants>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\LICENSE">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath></PackagePath>
    </None>
    <None Include="..\agpl-3.0.txt">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath></PackagePath>
    </None>
    <None Include="..\NOTICE">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath></PackagePath>
    </None>
    <None Include="..\README.md">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath></PackagePath>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>
  
</Project>
